-- title:
--   Base change of the flat deformation condition along a local homomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative local rings with $B$ having finite residue field, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring equipped with algebra structures on both $A$ and $B$, and let $\varphi \colon A \to B$ be a ring homomorphism that is local (non-units go to non-units). Let $\rho$ be an object of [`GaloisRepAdic A`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is, a free finite $A$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_A V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$) to $\mathrm{End}_A V$ that is continuous for the $\mathfrak{m}_A$-adic topology in the sense of [`GaloisActionIsAdicContinuous`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L9). Let $p$ be a natural number and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers, and suppose [`GaloisRep.flatCondition 𝒪 p S`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L47) holds for $\rho$: the determinant is cyclotomic at $p$ (that is, $p \in \mathfrak{m}_A$, and whenever $\sigma$ acts on the $p^n$-th roots of unity by the $a$-th power, $\det \rho(\sigma) - a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$), $\rho$ is flat at $p$ in the sense of [`GaloisRepAdic.IsFlatAt`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L29) (the residue field of $A$ is finite, and for every ideal $I$ with $A/I$ finite the $I$-level quotient $V/IV$ is, Galois-equivariantly, the group of points of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8)), and $\rho$ is unramified at every prime $q \notin S$. Then the same three conditions hold for the base change $\rho.\text{baseChangeAlong}\ \varphi$, whose module is $B \otimes_A V$ with $\sigma$ acting by the base change of $\rho(\sigma)$. The ring $\mathcal{O}$ and the two $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structures occur only as parameters of the predicate; $\varphi$ is not required to be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map.
--
--   This is the functoriality of the flat deformation condition of type $S$ under base change along local homomorphisms of coefficient rings, the property needed for [`GaloisRep.flatCondition`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L47) to serve as a deformation condition in the sense of Mazur. It is used in the construction of the flat deformation rings and of the associated patching data in the modularity-lifting argument.
-- source:
